. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * 
. ** UPDATE: We only employ random effects model instead of employing both rand
> om and fixed effects models **
. 
.         /* We consider political left-right self-placement (plh0004) as a goo
> d measure of left-leaning preferences. We reverse the direction of the variab
> le so that higher value denotes more left-leaning preferences (on a scale fro
> m 0 to 10).
>         
>         The dependent variables are availabe in four years: 2005, 2009, 2014,
>  2019. We run random effects linear regresion analysis with plh0004 as depend
> ent variable, applying robust standard errors. Our independent variable kidse
> x_all has three categories denoting whether having biological daughters in th
> e survey year: `No daughter', `Only daughter(s), and `Mixed'. 
>         
>         We also include the following control variables: gender, age group, e
> ducation, employment status, net household income, marital status, number of 
> biological children, whether youngest biological child <= 3 years, region (We
> st or East Germany), and migration background.
>         */
.         
.         xtset pid syear

Panel variable: pid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2005 to 2019, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

.         
